### Acceptance mapping
- After save, `events.config.prizes[*]` has no `unitCost`/`vendorSponsored` ✅ (stripped)
- Reload shows saved values ✅ (load maps `prize_costs` back onto state)
- A `prize_costs` error does not change `state.prizes` ✅ (error check leaks nothing; the catch path that resets prizes is never entered)

### Anything I was unsure about
- The **vendor checkbox label uses a general-purpose `.field-allow-other` class** (checked-box style) rather than new dedicated CSS — it matched the intended look and kept the diff smaller; the "ราคา/ชิ้น" box itself uses new `.cost-*` classes.
- I decided to **block** the save on invalid price (task says invalid "block save") rather than the looser "on cost-upsert error config save still counts" — both requirements are in the text; it reads that cost-value errors block, while the write failing still counts. If you'd prefer invalid prices to save (leaving the row unset) instead of blocking, that's a one-line change.
- I could not run `bash supabase/tests/run.sh` (needs Docker, per instructions — Claude runs it). I only touched `admin.html`, no schema/JS module files changed.
